# (build 104) The planet is set by every level load, as LoadLevelData does
# (ps2.asm:13229: planet_index = bit 7 of the level record's first byte).
#
# routes/saves/zosa_bareheaded.json is story_skure.json -- the party in
# Zosa, under its Data Memory's door (21,5) -- with Rolf's Magic Cap
# taken off by hand (it stays in his bag). Like every save the port made
# on Dezolis before build 104, it says "planet": "Motavia": the port never
# set the planet on a level load, so it stayed what the last save said.
#
# CONTINUE puts the party in Zosa; the Data Memory's door, walked into
# bareheaded, runs CheckPlanetAndCaps (loc_B44A, ps2.asm:16573): on
# Dezolis a live Rolf without the Magic or Mogic Cap is refused, "Danyaraha?
# bebekucha?" ($810). Before build 104 the port took Zosa for Motavia and
# said "Welcome to Data Memory." ($301).

start slot 1 routes/saves/zosa_bareheaded.json
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait screen level
wait idle
expect level $0B 21 6
walk up 1
wait screen building
wait idle
expect script $0810          # "Danyaraha? bebekucha?"
shot 01_refused
